{
  "id": "survivor-deleted-concurrently",
  "title": "The survivor of a merge is deleted by a device that had not seen the duplicate",
  "covers": [
    "ticket follow-up 4: a concurrent note.deleted on the survivor hides the duplicate's cards",
    "ticket follow-up 3: a delete racing a duplicate depends on arrival order"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "B adds 食べる offline (note L, T+20) and reviews its card. A, also offline, deletes its old note W for the same word (T+25).",
    "B syncs first: L is merged into W, L's card into W's card.",
    "A syncs: W is tombstoned. Its cards are hidden with it, including the card that now carries B's review. The word is gone from the queue on both devices; B's review stays in review_log.",
    "Had A synced FIRST, W would no longer have been live when L arrived: no collision, no merge, and L would have lived on. The outcome depends on arrival order at the server; every replica still converges on the server's verdict. Accepted trade-off."
  ],
